Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] i2c: qcom-cci: initialize reset completions without a bus node

cci_reset() and the reset interrupt use master[0].irq_complete even if
only i2c-bus@1 is available. Initialize completions for all hardware
masters before setting up bus adapters or requesting the interrupt.

Prepared against Linux v7.2.9, original source SHA-256:
9b189c25a295b6093041f659047cf7120d67030e657ba08183e4b3d7fcadc41d
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gregkh/linux/v7.2.9/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c

Status: source applicability and native 7.2.9 module build verified;
hardware untested and unloaded.
The PZ13 became unreachable during the bus@1-only live experiment. This
defect is a plausible cause; the recovered journal ends before the probe and
contains no later failure trace.
Not installed, submitted upstream, or added to the normal boot.

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -520,6 +520,10 @@
 	if (!cci->data)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
+	/* Controller-wide reset uses master 0 even when its bus is absent. */
+	for (i = 0; i < cci->data->num_masters; i++)
+		init_completion(&cci->master[i].irq_complete);
+
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(dev->of_node, child) {
 		struct cci_master *master;
 		u32 idx;
@@ -559,7 +563,6 @@
 				master->mode = I2C_MODE_FAST_PLUS;
 		}
 
-		init_completion(&master->irq_complete);
 	}
 
 	/* Memory */
